   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.3. Increased capacity of Member States to formulate and implement policies for a just transition towards environmentally sustainable economies and societies</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2023 the Government of Botswana and Social Partners  adopted a Tripartite Action Plan on Just Transition. The Action Plan seeks to inform national development strategies and inspire the tripartite actors to design and implement just transition strategies and policies towards Addressing Climate Change and Promoting a Just Transition to a Greener World of Work in Botswana. During the biennium  the ILO through funding from the RBSA Project on &quot;Addressing Climate Change and Promoting a Just Transition to a Greener World of Work in Botswana&quot; supported a series of capacity building workshop for the tripartite constituents on the development on Just Transition towards a greener world of work in Botswana.  In September 20023 , twenty-five representatives of the labour federations and 20 representatives from employers&apos;&apos; organizations   participated in in a workshop on the development of the Tripartite.</narrative>
   </description>
